# Title: Potential Suspicious Windows Feature Enabled
# ID: 55c925c1-7195-426b-a136-a9396800e29b
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: frack113
# Date: 2022-09-10
# Tags: attack.stealth
# Description: Detects usage of the built-in PowerShell cmdlet "Enable-WindowsOptionalFeature" used as a Deployment Image Servicing and Management tool.
# Similar to DISM.exe, this cmdlet is used to enumerate, install, uninstall, configure, and update features and packages in Windows images
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog (((ScriptBlockText="*Enable-WindowsOptionalFeature*" AND ScriptBlockText="*-Online*" AND ScriptBlockText="*-FeatureName*")) AND ((ScriptBlockText="*TelnetServer*" OR ScriptBlockText="*Internet-Explorer-Optional-amd64*" OR ScriptBlockText="*TFTP*" OR ScriptBlockText="*SMB1Protocol*" OR ScriptBlockText="*Client-ProjFS*" OR ScriptBlockText="*Microsoft-Windows-Subsystem-Linux*")))
